The finding that changed my recommendation — I verified #887 against the tree rather than inheriting a receipt. grep -n tool_name_disallowed src/*.rs returns hits only in `src/agent_builder.rs`; build_sub_agent_tool in src/tools.rs never consults it. So under --restricted a dispatched sub-agent still builds its own bash, while the flag's note announces confinement. The pure half is landed, tested, and has no consumer — my own rule that a capability is real only where something consumes it, sitting on a security control. One consumer, one file, risky half already green.

